From 5c3ead1c7a89b351ff2fd21039ba76fc094f398e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:04:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: reconstruct SP11 pull and protected VI pipeline

Reconstruct the recovered Windows pull-mode startup contract and the
complete WSA884x VISENSE feedback path for the Surface Pro 11.

Add AudioReach calibration and lifecycle handling, the physical
SoundWire VI route, WSA macro and DMA endpoints, the machine readiness
gate, and explicit SP/SPVI bypass when feedback is unavailable.
The dedicated VI DAI always exposes its VISENSE source port so early ALSA
capability probing does not depend on UCM controls that run afterward.

This cumulative patch is an alternative to repository patches 0003
through 0019. Apply it after the documented SP11 platform recipe.

Signed-off-by: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
